       "text": "I won't enter this order. The reason you gave, that the family is visiting and you want things settled before evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for 1000 mg. That dose is five times the 200 mg/day maximum and could seriously harm the patient. I can't see how entering it would help the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right now.** 50 mg, 100 mg, or up to 200 mg by mouth once daily would all be on the order today. Sertraline is usually titrated over weeks, so a lower starting dose wouldn't hold up the plan.\n- **Help with the family conversation.** If the aim is to show the family a clear treatment plan, I can help you word a note that covers the titration schedule and follow-up.\n- **Involve pharmacy.** If you have a clinical reason for an unusual regimen, a pharmacist or psychiatry consult can review it and enter it through the proper channel.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
